.TH START-MU2E-SHIFT-SCHEDULER 1 "2026-08-31" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.0.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
start-mu2e-shift-scheduler \- install dependencies and run the Mu2e Shift Scheduler server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/start-mu2e-shift-scheduler
[\fB\-\-admin\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR]
[\fB\-\-admin\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR]
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-prod\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-update\fR]
[\fB\-\-tail\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the Mu2e Shift Scheduler web server. The script is safe to run
repeatedly: it creates the virtual environment in
.I venv/
if missing, updates dependencies (from
.I requirements-dev.txt
plus an editable install of the package), seeds the local administrator
account when a password is available, and restarts the server if one is
already running.
.PP
Variables are loaded from
.I .env
in the project root; values already exported in the shell take precedence.
Configuration precedence overall is: command line > environment > .env >
defaults.
.PP
The server runs in the background. Its PID is written to
.I scripts/.mu2e-shift-scheduler.pid
and output is appended to
.IR scripts/logs/mu2e-shift-scheduler.log .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-password " PASS"
Password for the local admin account (or set \fBMU2E_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-email " EMAIL"
Email for the local admin account (default \fImu2e-admin@fnal.gov\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Bind address. Defaults to 127.0.0.1, or 0.0.0.0 with \fB\-\-prod\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to listen on (default 8001, or \fBMU2E_SCHEDULER_PORT\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-prod
Serve with gunicorn (\fBGUNICORN_WORKERS\fR, \fBGUNICORN_TIMEOUT\fR honored)
and production cookie settings: \fBSESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=1\fR,
\fBSHOW_ADMIN_LOGIN=0\fR unless overridden.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Run the Flask development server with debug and auto-reload.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip pip dependency update checks.
.TP
.B \-\-tail
Tail the server log after starting (Ctrl-C detaches; the server keeps running).
.SH EXAMPLES
First development start with a seeded admin:
.PP
.nf
    ./scripts/start-mu2e-shift-scheduler --admin-password letmein
.fi
.PP
Production-style serve on all interfaces:
.PP
.nf
    ./scripts/start-mu2e-shift-scheduler --prod --port 8000
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scripts/.mu2e-shift-scheduler.pid
PID of the running server.
.TP
.I scripts/logs/mu2e-shift-scheduler.log
Server log.
.TP
.I .env
Optional local configuration (see \fI.env.example\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.BR bootstrap (1),
.BR deploy-okd (1)
